  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 321 PM MDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nFriday... Rain continues in the San Juans on Friday, but \ndegrading over the course of the day as moisture leaves the area\nand the low pressure center over CA splits. A Flood Watch \nremains in effect for the eastern San Juans through 0Z Saturday\nand the current end time looks to be on track. The plains stay \ndry through Friday with high temperatures climbing up into the \nlow to mid 80s. A sfc trough sets up over eastern CO which will \naid precipitation chances as we move into Saturday.\n\nSaturday into Sunday...The southern low will begin to deepen \nover AZ and help moisture return to CO. This moisture along with\nWAA and good synoptics will support more widespread \nprecipitation across the region. Light to moderate rain is \nexpected, but a locally heavy shower cannot be ruled out. WPC's \nDay 4 (Sat) Excessive Rain Outlook includes parts of SE CO in \nthe SLGT risk area. Day 5 also has part of the region in a SLGT \nrisk, but a much smaller area in far SE CO. There is the \npotential for flash flooding in areas which experience locally \nhigher rainfall totals for both Saturday and Sunday. Severe \nthunderstorms are not expected, given limited instability, but \nat least isolated to widely scattered thunder remains a\npossibility. The northern low will help push a cold front into \nCO on Saturday with high temperatures dropping into the 50s and \n60s in the plains. These colder temps will persist through the \nweekend and into Monday.\n\nFor the remainder of the period, generally dry with more\nseasonably type temperatures in place.",
